error[NK1306]: `mut` here marks the key of a map, and a key can't be changed in place.
  --> tests/a_for_mut_on_a_map_key_alone_is_refused.nika:8:10
   |
 8 |     for (mut k, v) in m {
   |          ^^^ marks the key
   |
   = note: The key decides where the entry stands in the map (its order, or its hash), so a key changed in place would leave the entry in the wrong place.
   = help: To change the values in place, write `mut` in front of the value alone: `for (k, mut v) in m`. To change a key, take the entry out and insert it again after the loop.
1 type error
